<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mpanzu a Kitima</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1509">1509</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mpanzu a Kitima was a Kongolese prince who contested the succession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-of-portugal">King João I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> in 1509 against his half-brother Afonso. Supported by opponents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, he was defeated in battle at the capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbanza-kongo">Mbanza Kongo</a>, a victory that Afonso attributed to the miraculous appearance of Saint James. Mpanzu was killed or executed after the battle.</p></div>
